function ignore value:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("discard", value)

function return value:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("return", value)

[a|] boolean means: @intrinsic("type", "bool")

true means: @intrinsic("cast", 1, a boolean)

false means: @intrinsic("cast", 0, a boolean)

[a|] pointer to pointee means: @intrinsic("add pointer depth", pointee)

value as destination means: @intrinsic("cast", value, destination)

flex section if condition:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("if", condition)

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] cell
    members:
        value

class:
    patterns:
        [an|] owner
    members:
        cell as a pointer to a cell

class:
    patterns:
        [an|] outcome
    members:
        owner as a pointer to an owner

class:
    patterns:
        [an|] envelope
    members:
        outcome

a concrete outcome containing {a pointer to an owner:owned} means: @intrinsic("construct", an outcome, owned)

an empty outcome means: @intrinsic("construct", an outcome, 0 as a pointer to an owner)

a concrete envelope containing {a pointer to an owner:owned} means: @intrinsic("construct", an envelope, a concrete outcome containing owned)

an empty envelope means: @intrinsic("construct", an envelope, an empty outcome)

to get the outcome for {a pointer to an owner:owned} when {boolean:condition}:
    if condition:
        return a concrete outcome containing owned
    return an empty outcome

to get the reversed outcome for {a pointer to an owner:owned} when {boolean:condition}:
    if condition:
        return an empty outcome
    return a concrete outcome containing owned

the selected outcome for {a pointer to an owner:owned} when {boolean:condition} means: @intrinsic("select", condition, a concrete outcome containing owned, an empty outcome)

the reversed selected outcome for {a pointer to an owner:owned} when {boolean:condition} means: @intrinsic("select", condition, an empty outcome, a concrete outcome containing owned)

to get the envelope for {a pointer to an owner:owned} when {boolean:condition}:
    if condition:
        return an empty envelope
    return a concrete envelope containing owned

the selected outcome array for {a pointer to an owner:owned} when {boolean:condition} means: @intrinsic("select", condition, [an empty outcome], [a concrete outcome containing owned])

@intrinsic("store", value, @intrinsic("construct", a cell, 41))
@intrinsic("store", pointer, @intrinsic("address of", value))
@intrinsic("store", object, @intrinsic("construct", an owner, pointer))
@intrinsic("store", reference, @intrinsic("address of", object))
ignore the outcome for reference when true
ignore the outcome for reference when false
ignore the reversed outcome for reference when true
ignore the reversed outcome for reference when false
ignore the selected outcome for reference when true
ignore the selected outcome for reference when false
ignore the reversed selected outcome for reference when true
ignore the reversed selected outcome for reference when false
ignore the envelope for reference when true
ignore the envelope for reference when false
ignore the selected outcome array for reference when true
ignore the selected outcome array for reference when false
